{
  // tsconfig.sw.json — the service worker, which is neither a browser module nor
  // a Worker module.
  //
  // sw.js runs in a ServiceWorkerGlobalScope: `skipWaiting`, `clients` and
  // `registration` are globals there and exist in NO other environment, which is
  // why it needs lib.webworker. That lib cannot share a program with lib.dom —
  // the two declare conflicting globals, which is the same collision
  // tsconfig.browser.json's own header documents about workers-types.
  //
  // A fourth program for one 15-line file looks like overkill until you name the
  // alternative: excluding it from the glob, which is exactly the allowlist habit
  // that let ten client islands go unchecked. One file, checked, in the only
  // environment where its globals are real.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "target": "esnext",
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["esnext", "webworker"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    // Two control-flow checks, set here because they are set in tsconfig.json
    // and a program is only as strict as its own options. Both cost nothing:
    // +0 diagnostics on every one of the ten programs, measured 2026-08-27.
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    // strictNullChecks ON, and this was the one program in config/ without it.
    // The header above argues why sw.js needs a SEPARATE program, which is a
    // claim about its globals; nothing here ever argued for a laxer one, and
    // the omission read as a decision because it sat where a decision goes.
    // 0 diagnostics under it, measured 2026-08-27. `strict` stays off for the
    // reason every other config in this directory gives: it bundles
    // noImplicitAny, 7,197 diagnostics of annotation labour repo-wide, which
    // would bury the checks that find bugs under the ones that find missing
    // annotations.
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "strict": false
  },
  "include": ["../src/client/sw.js", "../src/client/sw-globals.d.ts"]
}
